================================================================
 IMMUTABILITY TEST - attacking our own backups on purpose
================================================================
 run at (UTC) : 2026-07-30T15:54:58Z
 target       : a disposable canary object. Real assets are not touched.
----------------------------------------------------------------
A - how the buckets are actually configured on the server
$ mc retention info --default gf/gf-ai-worm
Object locking 'COMPLIANCE' is configured for 30DAYS.
$ mc retention info --default gf/gf-ai-gov
Object locking 'GOVERNANCE' is configured for 30DAYS.
$ mc version info gf/gf-ai-worm
gf/gf-ai-worm versioning is enabled

Object Lock requires versioning, and it can only be switched on when a bucket
is CREATED. 'mc mb --with-lock' is a one-way door. You cannot add it later to a
bucket you already have.
