G - the contrast: the GOVERNANCE bucket has a deliberate escape hatch
$ mc rm --version-id a37cfc4d-e325-47df-85bb-ca48d2444980 <gov canary>             # ordinary delete
    mc: <ERROR> Failed to remove `gf/gf-ai-gov/canary/canary-2026-07-30T15-54-58Z.txt`. Object, 'canary/canary-2026-07-30T15-54-58Z.txt (Version ID=a37cfc4d-e325-47df-85bb-ca48d2444980)' is WORM protected and cannot be overwritten
PASS  GOVERNANCE also refuses an ordinary version delete - it is a real lock
$ mc rm --bypass --version-id a37cfc4d-e325-47df-85bb-ca48d2444980 <gov canary>    # privileged and deliberate
    Removed `gf/gf-ai-gov/canary/canary-2026-07-30T15-54-58Z.txt` (versionId=a37cfc4d-e325-47df-85bb-ca48d2444980).
PASS  GOVERNANCE bypass ALLOWED - the same call that was refused in attack 2
      This is the capability we keep on purpose: a member asking us to delete
      their document, or a password accidentally committed to a prompt file.
